Most importantly, never feel ashamed about having a period at school or college. Menstruation is a normal biological process, and needing a sanitary pad is no different from needing any other personal-care product.

If your periods are consistently so heavy or painful that they interfere with attending classes, studying, or participating in activities, talk to a healthcare professional.

With a small emergency kit, regular pad changes, good hygiene, and a little preparation, managing periods at school or college can become much less stressful.
